## 34. Release needs every outgoing quantity and condition

Create and confirm `Cy Release Conditions`, `09170001034`, with a package that generates checklist items. On Checklist & Release, leave one outgoing condition blank and try release; then enter conditions but leave a quantity incomplete and try again.

Both incomplete attempts must fail. Fill each expected quantity and condition, save, and verify one release succeeds with matching Released history.

## 35. Outgoing quantity cannot exceed the expected quantity

Create a booking with a checklist item whose expected quantity is known. Try to release one more than expected, then correct it to the exact expected quantity.

The oversized quantity must be rejected. The valid quantity should save, and a failed attempt must not create a release or history row.

## 36. Return quantity cannot exceed the released quantity

For a booking with equipment released, open Return Inspection. Enter a returned quantity greater than the released quantity and attempt to save/finalize.

Expected: the return is rejected with a clear validation message. Correct the quantity and confirm the invalid attempt did not leave a partial Returned history entry.

## 37. A short return must be documented as Missing

For a released checklist item, enter a returned quantity lower than the released quantity but leave its status as Inspected. Attempt final review.

The review must fail until the short quantity is marked Missing and the condition/notes document what did not return. Then verify the complete review can proceed.

## 38. Return inspection values must match the allowed conditions

For a released booking, inspect every row and test Good, Minor Damage, Damaged, Missing, and Unwashed where appropriate. Try a value outside the allowed list or “Not Applicable.”

Expected: allowed values save consistently; invalid values are not offered and are rejected by the server if submitted. Verify saved conditions remain after reopening the Return Inspection tab.

## 39. Notification links open the matching booking tab

Create one due booking that reaches Awaiting Completion and another that reaches Awaiting Payment. Open each action-required notification from the bell.

The first must open its own booking on **Return Inspection**. The second must open its own booking on **Payments**. Verify the booking reference, customer, status, and tab all match the notification clicked.

## 40. Offline booking and payment replay without duplicates

With the admin app loaded and signed in, go offline and create `Dee Retry Test`, `09170001040`, with a new manual booking and payment. Verify both appear in the pending sync list. Reconnect, use **Sync Now**, then use it again after the first sync completes.

Verify one server booking, one linked payment, and correct local-to-server IDs after retry and refresh. No duplicate customer, booking, payment, checklist, or history record should appear. If the first sync reports a failure, retry it and confirm the same result.

